{
  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "The current best (config_029, acc 0.7250) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted in a multiprofile multimodal setup. All other design dimensions have been well-characterized (scvi_n200 >> scgpt, vit_l > resnet50, transformer > avgpool, weighted ≥ concat, multiprofile >> singleprofile). The only untested RNA encoder in this otherwise-optimal pipeline is pca_n2000. Config_012 tests whether a linear PCA encoder can match or approach scvi_n200's performance when paired with the best image encoder, aggregation, and fusion. This is high-value because: (1) it reduces uncertainty about the RNA encoder choice—the most impactful single variable (scgpt dropped accuracy to 0.52, scvi_n200 to 0.72); (2) if PCA performs comparably, it offers a cheaper alternative; (3) with only 2 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out PCA in the top pipeline is more informative than re-testing known-inferior variants (resnet50, avgpool, concat). Expected cost: moderate, likely slightly below config_029's 3.60 GPU hours since PCA encoding is lighter than scVI, roughly 3.0–3.5 GPU hours."
}

